  "query_preview": "..\n\nNext 7 days (Through next Tuesday)...\n\nEarly this morning, scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms \nwill linger over central and eastern Montana as the broad upper \nlow exits the region. As this activity comes to an end, mostly dry\nconditions will prevail today, though there is a slight chance \nfor showers (15 percent) or weak thunderstorms (10 percent) over \nthe mountains in south- central Montana this evening. The chance \nof precipitation then increases over south-central Montana tonight\n(15 to 30 percent) as our next weather system approaches the \narea. Thursday, the chance of precipitation spreads across the \narea (40 to 60 percent).\n\nThursday afternoon and evening will see another round of \nscattered thunderstorms, with some possibly becoming strong to \nsevere over south-central/eastern Montana and north- \ncentral/eastern Wyoming. With this, the Storm Prediction Center \ncurrently has locations around and east of Billings under a \nMarginal Risk (level 1 of 5) with far southeastern Montana under a\nSlight Risk (level 2 of 5).\n\nUpper level ridging builds over the region Friday, allowing for \nwarm and mostly dry conditions into early Saturday. A strong \nPacific storm system is taking shape for the PacNW heading into \nthe weekend and our area will come under increasing southwest flow\naloft with a period of energy pushing over the area. This pattern\nis a favorable one for shower/thunderstorm development with the \npotential to move low level plains moisture deep into our area \nunder a strongly sheared atmosphere. A cold front is forecast late\nSaturday into Sunday, which will provide additional focus for \nconvective development. Some models have trended towards an \nearlier timing for the frontal passage, which may limit high \ntemperatures and somewhat limit thunderstorm development Saturday.\nStay up to date with the forecast if you have outdoor plans this \nweekend. Early next week currently looks to remain unsettled.\n\nHigh temperatures will increase from mostly 70s today to mostly \n80s by Friday. Saturday looks to be the warmest day of the week \nwith highs in the 80s to lower 90s, warmest over eastern Montana. \nHigh temperatures Sunday will be cooler in the upper 60s and 70s \nbehind the cold front passage. Temperatures trend warmer again\nearly next week. Archer/LA",
